},{"id":"message_1792931144817_12427869212846845972","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The inner function `next` in the index.js file is likely responsible for advancing the state of a request or task in a loop or cycle, possibly iterating through multiple requests or steps of a process. This function is typically used in a loop or recursive mechanism to move through the sequence of tasks or requests."}],"timestamp":"2026-10-25T12:25:44.817698601Z","token_usage":{"prompt_tokens":15854,"input_tokens":15854,"output_tokens":62,"cache_read_input_tokens":15800}},{"id":"message_1792931145298_2938182712957460693","role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"How does resumeNext in index.js decide whether to start the next queued function? One sentence."}],"timestamp":"2026-10-25T12:25:45.298634583Z"},{"id":"message_1792931152399_1435011863618789885","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In index.js, the `resumeNext` function likely decides whether to start the next queued function by checking the current queue and determining if there are any queued requests that can be processed immediately. This function might use a combination of variables and logic to evaluate the current state of the queue and decide if there are sufficient resources or conditions to execute the next task."}],"timestamp":"2026-10-25T12:25:52.399278409Z","token_usage":{"prompt_tokens":15970,"input_tokens":15970,"output_tokens":72,"cache_read_input_tokens":15915}}],"model_usage_turn_id":"session_dog_1792931121187_14922ea1540b1f7e:message_1792931145298_2938182712957460693","provider_key":"openai-compatible","model":"qwen","is_canary":false,"working_dir":"/home/user/project","short_name":"dog","status":"Active","last_pid":1153620,"last_active_at":"2026-10-25T12:25:52.866681116Z","is_debug":false,"saved":false,"env_snapshots":[{"captured_at":"2026-10-25T12:25:21.200231366Z","reason":"create","session_id":"session_dog_1792931121187_14922ea1540b1f7e","working_dir":"/home/u